Wed Jan 21 15:39:21 UTC 2026 - John Paul Adrian Glaubitz <adrian.glaubitz@suse.com>

- Packaging improvements:
  * Pass main.version=%{version}
    (d:l:g maintainer: not recommended but keeping)
  * Build with CGO_ENABLED=0
    (d:l:g maintainer: defaults recommended but keeping, except on
    s390x armv6l armv7l where conflicts with:
    error: -buildmode=pie requires external (cgo) linking, but cgo is not enabled)
  * Re-enable go_modules service to create vendor.tar.xz
  * Use pushd/pop to change into build directory to accommodate
    unusual cmd/ dir having its own go.mod
  * Build PIE with pattern that may become recommended procedure:
    %%ifnarch ppc64 GOFLAGS="-buildmode=pie" %%endif go build
    A go toolchain buildmode default config would be preferable
    but none exist at this time.
  * Drop mod=vendor, go1.14+ will detect vendor dir and auto-enable
  * Drop Requires: golang-packaging. The recommended Go toolchain
    dependency expression is BuildRequires: golang(API) >= 1.x or
    optionally the metapackage BuildRequires: go
  * Use BuildRequires: golang(API) >= 1.24 matching go.mod

